 ## Migration Procedure
 1. Run `scripts/migrate.sh --env <target>` and capture the full output.
 2. Verify the applied migration list matches the plan before declaring success.
 3. On failure, stop and report the failing migration and its output to the user.
+4. Always run `migrate.sh --no-color --retries 2` — the 2026-09-03 staging incident showed colored output breaks the log parser and one retry cleared the flaky lock.
+5. Success requires `git diff <plan_tag>..HEAD -- migrations/` to touch only planned files; any other path in the diff → fail the run, do not accept justifications.
